{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 1.0,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["FCC2", "NAVC2"],
      "pins": ["FCC2.11", "FCC2.27", "FCC2.50", "FCC2.75", "FCC2.100", "NAVC2.19", "NAVC2.32", "NAVC2.48", "NAVC2.64"],
      "nets": ["unconnected-(FCC2-VDD-Pad11)", "unconnected-(NAVC2-VDD-Pad19)"],
      "observed": "The VDD pins of both MCUs are on unconnected nets in the netlist, not tied to any supply rail.",
      "expected": "They should be connected to the 3.3V rail, as the specification states 3V3 feeds both MCUs.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"216\") (name \"unconnected-(FCC2-VDD-Pad11)\") (node (ref \"FCC2\") (pin \"11\") (pinfunction \"VDD\") (pintype \"power_in\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"276\") (name \"unconnected-(NAVC2-VDD-Pad19)\") (node (ref \"NAVC2\") (pin \"19\") (pinfunction \"VDD\") (pintype \"power_in\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "3V3 feeds both MCUs (FCC, NAVC) and all I2C sensor ICs"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Both microcontrollers are unpowered, so the board cannot boot or function at all.",
      "confidence": 1.0
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["NAVC2"],
      "pins": ["NAVC2.18", "NAVC2.63"],
      "nets": ["Net-(NAVC2-VSS-Pad18)", "GND"],
      "observed": "NAVC2 VSS pins 18 and 63 are connected only to each other on net Net-(NAVC2-VSS-Pad18), which is not connected to the GND net.",
      "expected": "They should be connected to GND to provide a ground reference for the NAVC MCU.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"144\") (name \"Net-(NAVC2-VSS-Pad18)\") (node (ref \"NAVC2\") (pin \"18\") (pinfunction \"VSS\") (pintype \"power_in\")) (node (ref \"NAVC2\") (pin \"63\") (pinfunction \"VSS\") (pintype \"passive\")))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The NAVC microcontroller has no ground reference, so it cannot operate even if powered.",
      "confidence": 1.0
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["REG3", "FCC2", "NAVC2"],
      "pins": ["REG3.1", "REG3.2"],
      "nets": ["+3.3V", "+3V3"],
      "observed": "The netlist contains two separate 3.3V nets: +3.3V (LDO output and most sensors) and +3V3 (MCU pull-ups, switches, connectors, and NAVC2 VBAT), with no connection between them. The SPICE deck also models them as two independent voltage sources.",
      "expected": "A single 3.3V rail should feed both the MCUs and the sensors, as described in the specification.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"1\") (name \"+3.3V\") ... (node (ref \"REG3\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"OUT\")) ...)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"2\") (name \"+3V3\") ... (node (ref \"NAVC2\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"VBAT\")) ...)"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "V_3_3V +3.3V 0 DC 3.3\nV_3V3 +3V3 0 DC 3.3"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "3.3 V LDO ... produces 3V3 for \"MCUs and Sensors\""
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The LDO only powers the +3.3V net, leaving the +3V3 net unpowered. I2C pull-ups, MCU VBAT, and several connectors on +3V3 will not function, causing bus and power failures even if the MCUs were otherwise connected.",
      "confidence": 1.0
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain multiple severe power and ground connection anomalies: both MCUs have unconnected VDD pins, the NAVC ground pins are isolated from GND, and the 3.3V rail is split into two unconnected nets (+3.3V and +3V3). These deviations would prevent the board from operating as intended."
}

